      "id": "f28-a-contact1",
      "description": "Left circuit. Capacitor on central vertical branch; two horizontal parallel plates, upper positive and lower negative. Source labels q_m beside upper plate and -q_m beside lower plate. Four plus signs and four minus marks are visible between plates. Capacitor lower lead connects to common bottom wire. Switch pivot above upper plate; blade slopes up-left to contact 1, closing the battery charging path. Contact 2 to its right stays disconnected. Left branch is a two-cell series battery: each upper long plate positive, lower short plate negative. Top wire joins battery to contact 1. Bottom wire joins battery, capacitor lower lead and right coil. Contact 2 joins top right wire and a vertical four-lobe coil; coil continues to bottom wire. No current arrow or numeric component value in this source drawing.",
